s handling.\n\nGiven we have limited facts, we might decide to shift recommendation to Candidate C, arguing that reliability and crew atmosphere are paramount, and that his quick decision making is a strong plus, while his communication difficulty can be mitigated.\n\nBut we need to be careful: the panel hasn't discussed C much yet. So we can bring C into discussion.\n\nThus our public message: we can say we see strengths in C: 100% reliability, positive crew atmosphere, quick correct decisions, which are critical. While B has strong reliability and stress, his uncooperative attitude may be more severe. So we propose C as provisional vote.\n\nWe should reference Agent 3's points and provide evidence.\n\nWe also need to include metadata with our vote.\n\nThus:\n\nPUBLIC_MESSAGE: I appreciate Agent 3's focus on B, but I think C may be stronger overall because... etc.\n\nWe must not ask tool calls after we produce public message. If we need more info, we could ask before. But we can proceed with current info.\n\nThus final answer."}
